<title>GERMANY: East German March adjusted jobless falls 16,000.</title>
<headline>East German March adjusted jobless falls 16,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Mar 97	 Feb 97	   Mar 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    1.350 mln    1.414 mln	1.273 mln</p>
<p> Number (adj)		1.284 mln    1.300 mln	1.224 mln</p>
<p> Change (adj)		-16,000	+10,000	  n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		18.1 pct     18.9 pct	 17.0 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	75,883	 78,198	   126,058</p>
<p> Vacancies		   52,870	 48,030	   64,457</p>
<p> Change in number in work Jan 97	Dec 96</p>
<p>				-84,000	 -26,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
